pe {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312640} :answer-field/id #uuid "84f3fd45-186b-54c5-b25c-e6e9e5466871" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e36a242-eb33-5726-9cd8-f7cfed1a28c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312077} {:answer/id #uuid "ccac23c7-1da0-504c-ac7d-1a8968f5eac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313576} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1058b4-6376-5586-bc33-0b23121b9e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313583} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f4fa5d-385b-51f0-bf04-00d74719c3de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313925} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6979c8-a190-541f-9b05-38103a570d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb6979c8-a190-541f-9b05-38103a570d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313981} :answer-field/id #uuid "a925a809-38ca-5726-b5c0-4b10936b7bd4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6e1060a-5b44-588b-92cb-8c6f7184af4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-340732" :question/problem "Complete the arguments in the reasoning below to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{t/2}.$First, we apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=F(s)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nWe now examine the convergence of $F(s)$ for different values of $s:$\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-2}}\nthe integral is divergent.\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-3}}\nthe integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating our integral in the convergent case, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $L{{e}^{t/2}}=\\frac{2}{2s-1},$ \ndefined for\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(t)$ defined on $[0,\\infty ),$ the Laplace transform of $f,$ denoted $L{f(t)}$ or $F(s),$ is a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{t/2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{t/2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st+t/2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne \\frac{1}{2}$ or $s=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- If $s\\ne \\frac{1}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(1/2-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{1/2-s}{e}^{(1/2-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1/2-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/2}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/2}-\\frac{1}{s-1/2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=\\frac{1}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{1}{2}) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(1/2-1/2)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s\\le \\frac{1}{2}$ the integral is divergent.\n\n- For $s>\\frac{1}{2}$ the integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>\\frac{1}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s-1/2}-\\frac{1}{s-1/2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(1/2-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/2}-\\frac{1}{s-1/2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2s-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{t/2}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{2}{2s-1},$ defined for $s>\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5095678a-8104-56eb-8831-1b6c9fac495a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le -\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312629} {:answer/id #uuid "ec563699-02b5-5e63-b1ca-96229eefc62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec563699-02b5-5e63-b1ca-96229eefc62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313863} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3a3120-35ca-5b04-92f4-497a276f7541" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/i