b/id #edb/ref 17592186312794} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e42ecc-59bc-5bc2-8c08-b7c60669b503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le -\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313300} {:answer/id #uuid "d160e714-5c7b-569c-b90b-3a6248ee49c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313611} {:answer/id #uuid "e55e1719-7063-579d-8557-74da7489a611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313788} {:answer/id #uuid "ea32d01e-b8ff-59fa-9782-c2fb47dcd2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8e42ecc-59bc-5bc2-8c08-b7c60669b503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\le -\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313300} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf059f47-58a0-5753-b1d2-f7dca1fe25f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc7c5db0-02db-5d4a-bb26-bb53af87d850" :question/math-academy-id "q-340733" :question/problem "Complete the arguments in the reasoning below to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-t/4}.$First, we apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=F(s)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nWe now examine the convergence of $F(s)$ for different values of $s:$\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-2}}\nthe integral is divergent.\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-3}}\nthe integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating our integral in the convergent case, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $L{{e}^{-t/4}}=\\frac{4}{4s+1},$ \ndefined for\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(t)$ defined on $[0,\\infty ),$ the Laplace transform of $f,$ denoted $L{f(t)}$ or $F(s),$ is a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{-t/4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st-t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne -\\frac{1}{4}$ or $s=-\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- If $s\\ne -\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{-1/4-s}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1/4-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>-\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=-\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-\\frac{1}{4}) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-(-1/4))t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s\\le -\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is divergent.\n\n- For $s>-\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>-\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4s+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-t/4}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{4}{4s+1},$ defined for $s>-\\frac{1}{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049bd69e-63f5-5d6a-a7fd-6e05487ff7ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311997} {:answer/id #uuid "2d66dc80-20c0-5256-961e-680a295ed14b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-F(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312333} {:answer/id #uuid "45ad3690-7e52-5880-8aaa-79998267a041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312544} {:answer/id #uuid "47a5e4c3-bf82-5a99-bfbc-ba3c896d145a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312556} {:answer/id #uuid "ef38ae32-9440-57b4-9e8a-dbf11b0cbcf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-s{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47a5e4c3-bf82-5a99-bfbc-ba3c896d145a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312556} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c1d0f20-2faa-5f5f-a89b-8d65340bd0d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "048eea09-5434-51cc-b74f-ea251e4d2e55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311996} {:answer/id #uuid "49926c57-f2e7-52eb-a771-546d17beca80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312567} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f340de-50f7-5ccf-a99f-7497970407e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}-16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313504} {:answer/id #uuid "c73a903a-47cb-59c3-a09f-3ddda8ddb812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313530} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a8f379-dfc3-565a-beaa-fb431017e2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49926c57-f2e7-52eb-a771-546d17beca80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312567} :answer-field/id #uuid "30f10b75-554e-546f-93fe-58fb3fa13441" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314142} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a16e49b-9015-582c-88ec-cf35086fbf11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312574} {:answer/id #uuid "cfce22d5-658b-5f7f-95cf-314e08330a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}-16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313600} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f36cde-7023-5dab-8390-2afebef3e36f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313791} {:answer/id #uuid "f407f16a-4db8-5043-aa7b-d9825bf06f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfce22d5-658b-5f7f-95cf-314e08330a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}-16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313600} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a224b5-09f2-53ac-9cda-3a12b1798324" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d929af9-eec8-568b-ad12-8c7a9c664c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312334} {:answer/id #uuid "3681bada-8bdc-51e7-ab58-ae7ef8438aed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312415} {:answer/id #uuid "810f4520-f645-5e3a-a3ee-b8e1e5bf8309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313014} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bf5cf5-aad6-5bed-8091-42b190f12f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4bf5cf5-aad6-5bed-8091-42b190f12f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313651} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1db4855-6479-5ff6-8518-b6f5bdd97377" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bc082e0-e258-5a86-b2f6-5e93b65fda0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340899" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\n \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t$ and $L{f(t)}=F(s).$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms,\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}={{field-4}},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=1,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}=-{F}^{′}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =4,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}) \\\\  & =({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}+s(-({s}^{2}+16)^{-2}\\cdot 2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}-\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}=-{F}^{′}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-16}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0393ece1-72d0-5a26-86d5-ccbeeaf37ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311992} {:answer/id #uuid "597f53c7-4437-514a-af3b-d52acd9b2c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312692} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa014c5-9b63-5c2d-9789-24fc078e3a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313121} {:answer/id #uuid "94ca3393-2d0c-5d35-8160-e4662eb26e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "597f53c7-4437-514a-af3b-d52acd9b2c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312692} :answer-field/id #uuid "38fae9d9-cbd3-5455-8427-b745a060a7d6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "664a4c96-a01f-59cb-967b-ffb4901c3599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312781} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5c2bf1-f5e6-5b17-9d72-cc0c282c3bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312999} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd2bb9a-325d-5590-893b-654f04aa3611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313092} {:answer/id #uuid "b056a71c-b807-5605-908f-a02ed7bf64a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313347} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cc3710-19e9-51a7-83aa-4c898958b227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0cc3710-19e9-51a7-83aa-4c898958b227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313485} :answer-field/id #uuid "a284234b-2957-5483-83fc-1e261cf48e0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b3b95d4-60c8-526c-96a6-a82f623ad04d" :question/math-academy-id "q-340932" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{4}+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}(0-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8aacf8a-923a-5706-a78c-108e65099a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8aacf8a-923a-5706-a78c-108e65099a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313826} :answer-field/id #uuid "55ac9af9-f5be-5aac-9b98-a73bb56de950" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f398213-9b43-5009-a712-5e39a192aab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f398213-9b43-5009-a712-5e39a192aab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312352} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e679c8-0512-5ea7-a995-5f08819c8352" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6db0058b-56f3-5a30-bae9-0cf86c420390" :question/math-academy-id "q-340945" :question/problem "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(2,2).$\n\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-16{x}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(2)=-\\frac{16}{(2)^{3}}=-\\frac{16}{8}=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{-2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2) \\\\ 2y-4 & =x-2 \\\\ x-2\\cdot y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "392b0b79-8325-51e9-80af-b0e2db96f3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "392b0b79-8325-51e9-80af-b0e2db96f3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312438} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aba0483-9c05-5996-9c78-df0105e89050" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f44134b3-2bb1-57f7-a413-41c3c3c73af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341011" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(4)-(\\frac{1}{2})(2)}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-1}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb50bd7f-39cc-56cb-aa5b-7218d902f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb50bd7f-39cc-56cb-aa5b-7218d902f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0182abb-5f03-5f80-a3dd-0dc6384897c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65226573-de55-55b8-bdde-6256c33bf52d" :question/math-academy-id "q-341013" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,g(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,{g}^{′}(4)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(4)g(4)-f(4){g}^{′}(4)}{(g(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-2\\cdot (-1)}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07634376-05f7-5c3f-a0aa-27add524b643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}+49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312024} {:answer/id #uuid "17ef972b-f314-526b-81aa-e2ce319165ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312145} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3a0c6b-7abe-5d48-aea0-64a847e3d2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}-49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312470} {:answer/id #uuid "4de4061e-d72d-5f53-83b8-8dc072e09abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de4061e-d72d-5f53-83b8-8dc072e09abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312609} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aaecc08-c488-5535-bed2-98e522543499" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175