92186312441} {:answer/id #uuid "ab5ee628-6197-5596-bd0c-cb3cf17c4546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-F(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313318} {:answer/id #uuid "d16b16f9-269e-56d8-847c-9242e7fc0377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16b16f9-269e-56d8-847c-9242e7fc0377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{F}^{′}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313612} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec379e4-6326-5470-b34e-2a9f7a36b67f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ab0471-9ab5-5d94-9472-9c9745ccd041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312385} {:answer/id #uuid "68430b40-6d63-5c5b-bafe-6b99044058d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312793} {:answer/id #uuid "d112e8a6-b00c-5763-974e-6a78131a0a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313608} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ddf551-1124-5b15-bae0-588313713cea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d112e8a6-b00c-5763-974e-6a78131a0a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313608} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe32a19-a038-5a1c-9adb-5fab337cee14" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed378e80-6795-5ad0-8973-5105f9a33be1" :question/math-academy-id "q-341050" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t}.\n$$\n\n \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>\\omega .\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t$ and $L{f(t)}=F(s).$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms,\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>7.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t}={{field-4}},\\,s>7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=1,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}=-{F}^{′}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =7,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49},\\,s>7.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s({s}^{2}-49)^{-1}) \\\\  & =({s}^{2}-49)^{-1}+s(-({s}^{2}-49)^{-2}\\cdot 2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}-\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-49-{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡7t}=-{F}^{′}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+49}{({s}^{2}-49)^{2}},\\,s>7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d1446c-0422-5804-ab35-51c287ebd71b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d8da40e-cfdf-5c60-a36a-cdb26f7bb8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-341104" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x+arccotx$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+arccotx) \\\\  & =2+(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}(0) & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "736358be-b15d-5572-9a7d-e2c1b162c5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312889} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d51f45-9ac3-50b7-8e7e-a99791f5df84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313397} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb7f8c7-f0ee-5b82-8e68-9bf292adfc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313448} {:answer/id #uuid "ca011ffd-4317-5cd0-a523-b8d946003250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313551} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2f2e3a-830c-5c61-97de-1eeed7ae62c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313580} {:answer/id #uuid "fd385b6a-f413-51e4-8c07-5e53e44b0516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "736358be-b15d-5572-9a7d-e2c1b162c5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312889} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97fbae0-d928-5e16-8119-2ca0e620f0dc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9aeaa1-b187-5b93-9a34-d4e755e38dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312170} {:answer/id #uuid "3de705a6-c93c-5847-aef8-686296cd036d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312475} {:answer/id #uuid "65422943-54ca-5806-b182-99db46b4b27f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312773} {:answer/id #uuid "67ae037d-6d7f-5de0-9976-57829f55953f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312789} {:answer/id #uuid "c98c24e1-c972-56c4-ba20-92ddfb1aa44c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3de705a6-c93c-5847-aef8-686296cd036d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312475} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddaee052-1803-54cd-a0f9-ce0838d40348" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2c45534-de22-5957-94a0-9fb0be556b3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341107" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)=\\frac{{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{2t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-2t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2 \\\\ L{{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+2},\\,s>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{2t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-2t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+2)+(s-2)}{(s-2)(s+2)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{2t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (2,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-2t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-2,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(2,\\infty )\\cap (-2,\\infty )=(2,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8edf9692-6828-531e-a524-456c401eb354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313116} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f609bf-30c3-5195-9625-8bf23dbeb98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313373} {:answer/id #uuid "c61fae7a-d115-5d60-aace-221720a5ea31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf692c6b-eaf1-58f2-b0cd-fa16ba85d66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313596} {:answer/id #uuid "e428bf77-631f-59d6-9120-f9ce05a41509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf692c6b-